#
# To promote: FIRST bump the version — package.al's `version`, the `current-seed-version` line in the
# CURRENT SEED block below, and scripts/package_cli_test.sh's expected `alatyr <version>` line. A
# compiler bakes the version of the tree it was COMPILED FROM (src/cli.al's cli_version reads the
# TOOL-15-injected app.version), so a Stage2 built before the bump answers the previous number for
# its whole life; that is #586, and the seed committed here is the proof.
# THEN build Stage1, have it build Stage2 and Stage3. Require Stage1 == Stage2 == Stage3 in
# the emitted GAS, byte-identical after normalizing the .L<N> and .Lra<N>_<k> label families (do
# that first, or the diff is drowned in renumbering), and Stage2 == Stage3 in the BINARY. Read the
# normalized seed->Stage1 GAS delta line by line, copy STAGE2 over seed/alatyr, append an entry to
# seed/HISTORY.md with those hashes and that delta reading, and re-run scripts/fixpoint.sh on the promoted tree —
# that run, not the label, is the proof.
#
# Stage2, and not all three binaries. Stage1 is assembled from the STALE seed's emission, so it
# implements the change for everything it compiles without carrying it in its own code; Stage2 is
# assembled from the new emission and carries it. Nor can Stage1's binary be made to match: a
# promotion also RELEASES A VERSION, so the promoted seed keeps a version string the Stage1 it
# builds from the same tree cannot carry until the next release. The 0.1.0 -> 0.2.0 promotion
# measured that difference as exactly 35 bytes, sizes equal, every one of them '1' -> '2'. The older
# wording here — "both the emitted GAS and the binary", "copy Stage1" — would have scored that
# successful promotion as a failed one, and the dated entries in seed/HISTORY.md have recorded Stage2 as the
# promoted stage all along.
#
# "Read the delta line by line" has a pass condition of its own: the delta must be describable in
# ONE SENTENCE. That promotion's was 822 hunks, 3288 lines added and zero removed — four lines per
# hunk, four distinguishable line shapes, every insertion immediately before a byte load whose
# index, length and pointer the three preceding lines set up. One recognizable pattern, repeated, is
# what a reviewable delta looks like. A delta that resists a one-sentence characterization is the
# signal to STOP and find out why.
#
# The promotion entries live in seed/HISTORY.md (#1130), and they are APPEND-ONLY: never rewrite them
# to make old hashes resolve. This file is the header and the CURRENT SEED block below.
